      content:
          '- **Presentation**: 6 weeks ago, acute onset severe low back pain while lifting weights at the gym. Progressive bilateral leg weakness over 12 hours. Noticed inability to urinate and numbness in the perineal region. Husband drove her to ED.\n- **Imaging**: MRI L-spine: massive L4-5 central disc herniation with severe cauda equina compression. Near-complete obliteration of the thecal sac.\n- **Surgical Course**: Emergent L4-5 laminectomy and discectomy performed 12 hours after symptom onset. Intraoperatively, the cauda equina was severely compressed with edematous nerve roots. Surgeon noted the roots were discolored but not transected.\n- **Post-operative Recovery**: Partial improvement. Leg strength improved from initial 1-2/5 bilaterally to current levels. Saddle numbness improved but persists. Urinary retention persists — started on clean intermittent catheterization (CIC) every 4-6 hours. Neurogenic bowel — requires scheduled bowel program.\n- **Current Functional Status**: Ambulatory with bilateral Lofstrand crutches. Can walk 500 feet before fatigue. Requires AFO on left (foot drop). Stairs with railing and supervision. Drives (automatic transmission, left foot weak but right foot functional for gas/brake). Independent in ADLs except needs extra time for toileting/catheterization.\n- **Bladder**: Areflexic bladder (LMN pattern). No sensation of fullness. CIC every 4-6 hours. Post-void residual >500 mL without catheterization. On tamsulosin 0.4 mg daily.\n- **Bowel**: Areflexic bowel (LMN pattern). No rectal sensation. Requires manual evacuation every other day. Uses stool softeners and bulk-forming agents.\n- **Sexual Function**: Complete loss of genital sensation. No clitoral sensation. No orgasm since injury. Reports vaginal dryness. Has not attempted intercourse since injury.\n- **PMH**: Previously healthy. Regular gym-goer. No prior back problems.\n- **Psychosocial**: Married 20 years. Two children ages 15 and 13. PE teacher — physically demanding job. Enjoys running, hiking, CrossFit (pre-injury). PHQ-9 score 14 (moderate depression).\n- **Medications**: Gabapentin 300 mg TID, tamsulosin 0.4 mg daily, docusate 100 mg BID, psyllium fiber daily, acetaminophen PRN.',
