      content:
          '**Longitudinal Follow-Up Protocol**:\n\n**Year 1 (Active Recovery Phase)**:\n- PM&R follow-up every 4-6 weeks for first 6 months, then every 3 months\n- PT/OT 2-3x weekly initially, tapering as strength plateaus\n- **Urodynamics** at 3 months and 12 months\n- Renal ultrasound at 12 months\n- EMG/NCS at 6 months if considering prognosis for ongoing recovery (can assess for reinnervation potentials)\n- Neuropsychological screening if depression persists\n- Vocational counseling for return to work planning\n\n**Annual Ongoing (Lifelong)**:\n- **Renal ultrasound annually**: Screen for hydronephrosis, stones\n- **Serum creatinine and urinalysis annually**: Monitor renal function\n- **Urodynamics every 2-3 years** or if symptoms change\n- **PM&R annual visit**: Reassess function, equipment needs, pain, bowel/bladder program effectiveness\n- **Urology co-management**: For complex bladder issues, recurrent UTIs, stones\n- **Gynecology**: Annual exam — discuss sexual function, pelvic floor health\n\n**Complication Surveillance**:\n- **UTIs**: Common with CIC. Educate on symptoms. Treat promptly.\n- **Renal deterioration**: The primary long-term threat. High-pressure bladder can cause reflux and kidney damage. Urodynamics detect this.\n- **Skin breakdown**: Saddle hypoesthesia means she may not feel pressure or irritation in the perineal area. Educate on skin inspection.\n- **Falls**: Ongoing fall risk from leg weakness. Annual reassessment of ambulatory aids and home safety.\n- **Psychological**: Depression, body image issues, sexual dysfunction — screen annually with PHQ-9. Offer counseling and support group referral.\n\n**Care Coordination Structure**:\n- **Physiatrist as medical home**: Coordinates all specialists, manages the rehabilitation plan, serves as longitudinal provider.\n- **Urology**: Bladder management, urodynamics, stone management.\n- **Colorectal/GI**: If bowel program becomes ineffective or incontinence worsens.\n- **Psychology/Psychiatry**: For depression and sexual health counseling.\n- **PCP**: Ongoing general health maintenance. Ensure PCP is educated about neurogenic bladder/bowel management.\n- **Employer/Occupational health**: ADA accommodations, return-to-work planning.',
